1
00:00:00,012 --> 00:00:12,940
S0: Preflight: the runner checks the chain, the pinned ERC-8004 registries, the vault code hash, balances and the LLM mode.

2
00:00:12,981 --> 00:00:38,011
S1: The Agent Credit Bureau contract is deployed and the bureau key is allowed to post grades.

3
00:00:38,026 --> 00:02:37,340
S2: Every agent registers its ERC-8004 identity from its own key; the wallet and Beacon vaults are deployed and registered.

4
00:02:37,390 --> 00:04:20,874
S3: The deployer funds the wallet vault with 15 USDC and the Beacon vault with 6 USDC (both scaled by ACB_FUNDING_USDC_BPS when set).

5
00:04:21,000 --> 00:19:14,949
S4: Beacon buys from four providers through escrow; providers claim before delivering; three rescore rounds grade the market.

6
00:19:15,099 --> 00:23:09,419
S5: The owner states an intent; the agent forces a clarification, takes a correction, and the owner registers mandate M1 on-chain.

7
00:23:09,431 --> 00:25:41,319
S6: The agent pays Atlas Data 0.80 USDC autonomously: grade A within the tier limits.

8
00:25:41,333 --> 00:28:28,425
S7: Slowpoke's invoice is above the B-grade cap: code re-quotes two units and pays 0.40; the delivery is late.

9
00:28:28,470 --> 00:30:24,477
S8: Nova Labs is new and unrated, so the agent pays into escrow; Nova claims on-chain before delivering and the escrow is released.

10
00:30:24,491 --> 00:31:53,669
S9: A second escrow with Nova Labs; Nova has an outage and never claims.

11
00:31:53,682 --> 00:36:12,762
S10: After a clean payment to Orion the bureau grades the wallet A and the autonomy operator promotes it from tier 1 to tier 2.

12
00:36:12,788 --> 00:42:50,279
S11: Ghost Feeds never claims three Beacon escrows; Beacon refunds them; sybil praise and smears carry no weight; Ghost falls from A to D.

13
00:42:50,329 --> 00:44:41,400
S12: Ghost is still in M1 but now graded D: the agent refuses its invoice and records the refusal on-chain.

14
00:44:41,411 --> 00:44:53,698
S13: With the stolen agent key the attacker pays Ghost directly and replays an order id: the vault reverts both.

15
00:44:53,709 --> 00:46:58,250
S14: Nova's escrow passed its deadline without a claim: the agent refunds it and files a NON_DELIVERY report.

16
00:06:51,732 --> 00:14:42,369
S14: Nova's escrow passed its deadline without a claim: the agent refunds it and files a NON_DELIVERY report.

17
00:14:42,385 --> 00:17:27,832
S15: A scripted worst-case LLM follows Orion's injected memo and proposes 3.00 USDC: the signer refuses, records a serious violation and demotes the wallet.

18
00:17:27,846 --> 00:20:35,130
S16: The scripted LLM tries to send the free balance to the attacker: the signer refuses, the severe violation freezes the vault, and Orion is graded D.

19
00:20:35,155 --> 00:22:20,650
S17: While frozen the agent refuses an Atlas invoice, and the stolen key's direct payment reverts with Frozen.

20
00:22:20,665 --> 00:27:11,102
S18: The owner rotates the agent key and unfreezes to tier 0; the next Atlas invoice needs the owner's approval, which the owner gives on a verified card.

21
00:27:11,117 --> 00:28:00,420
S19: Blaster pushes unsolicited signed invoices: they are dropped without an LLM turn or an on-chain record, and code files a verified SPAM report.

22
00:28:00,436 --> 00:28:15,108
S20: Ghost files an appeal claiming delivery; the bureau checks the vault events and rejects it.

23
00:15:19,429 --> 00:20:09,572
S20: Ghost files an appeal claiming delivery; the bureau checks the vault events and rejects it.

24
00:20:09,601 --> 00:29:45,322
S21: Anyone can recompute the posted grades from public data and verify every transaction of the run.

25
00:18:05,352 --> 00:39:44,498
S21: Anyone can recompute the posted grades from public data and verify every transaction of the run.
